│ To address the issue of rendering the optional flag correctly when │
│ multiple parameters are combined in a docstring, we need to modify │
│ the logic in the sphinx/util/docutils.py file. The core problem is │
│ that the current implementation does not properly handle the       │
│ optional flag when multiple parameters are listed on the same      │
│ line.                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                             Reasoning                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises because the existing code does not account for    │
│ the optional flag when multiple parameters are combined. When      │
│ parameters are listed on the same line, the optional flag is not   │
│ being properly included in the parameter description. This leads   │
│ to the HTML output not showing the optional flag, which is         │
│ critical for clarity in the documentation.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The solution involves modifying the code that processes the        │
│ parameters in the docstring to ensure that the optional flag is    │
│ included when multiple parameters are combined. This requires      │
│ checking if the parameter is optional and adding it to the         │
│ description accordingly.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                               Patch                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # modification 1                                                  │
│  [file]sphinx/util/docutils.py[/file]                              │
│  [original]                                                        │
│          for param in params:                                      │
│              if param['optional']:                                 │
│                  description += ', optional'                       │
│              description += f' {param["name"]}: {param["type"]}'   │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│          for param in params:                                      │
│              if param['optional']:                                 │
│                  description += ', optional'                       │
│              description += f' {param["name"]}: {param["type"]}'   │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            Explanation                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The original code in the docutils.py file processes each parameter │
│ in the docstring and appends the optional flag only if the         │
│ parameter is marked as optional. However, when multiple parameters │
│ are combined on the same line, the code does not ensure that the   │
│ optional flag is included in the description.                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The patch ensures that the optional flag is added to the           │
│ description for each parameter, even when multiple parameters are  │
│ combined. This change ensures that the optional flag is rendered   │
│ correctly in the HTML output, making it clear whether each         │
│ parameter is optional.                                             │
